  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We have exome variant calls for 160 lung adenocarcinoma patients, plus exon lengths, a cancer-gene list and the Hallmark GMT, and we'd like pathway mutation scores and 2 to 6 subtypes. I don't remember offhand whether the calls are somatic or germline."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"we'd like pathway mutation scores\" -- available from SAMBAR.\n2. \"2 to 6 subtypes\" -- available from SAMBAR.\n\n**SAMBAR**. SAMBAR reduces sparse mutation data to pathway-level scores with gene-length and, when configured, patient mutation-burden normalization. Patient distances and subtype labels depend on the downstream clustering settings; they are distinct from gene communities in a regulatory network. This is pathway aggregation followed by distance-based clustering, not non-negative matrix factorization; a mutation score does not establish permanent functional loss or equivalence of every mutation in a pathway.\n\nYou would need somatic mutation matrix, gene/exon-size CSV, cancer-gene list, GMT pathway file. The analysis would provide sample-by-gene mutation scores, not pathway scores; pathway-by-sample mutation scores, not cluster labels; sample-to-cluster labels, separate from score and distance matrices; pairwise sample distances, not cluster labels.\n\nTo use subtypes for chemotherapy resistance or another clinical outcome, you would also need outcome labels matched to the patients. Check cluster stability and confounding, then evaluate prediction on held-out patients. Fit feature selection and cohort-dependent network estimation within the training split to avoid information leakage.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
